## 7. Nodes

### 7.1 Node Feature Discovery (NFD)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Detects hardware features (CPU flags, PCI devices such as GPUs/NICs, kernel version, NUMA, SR-IOV capability) and labels nodes with `feature.node.kubernetes.io/*`. Prerequisite for GPU Operator, SR-IOV, and KMM; enables `nodeAffinity` scheduling on hardware. |
| **Package** | `nfd` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-nfd` / single namespace |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CR** | `NodeFeatureDiscovery`, `NodeFeatureRule` |

```yaml
apiVersion: nfd.openshift.io/v1
kind: NodeFeatureDiscovery
metadata: {name: nfd-instance, namespace: openshift-nfd}
spec:
  operand:
    image: registry.example.com:8443/openshift4/ose-node-feature-discovery-rhel9:v4.22   # mirrored path
    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
    servicePort: 12000
  workerConfig:
    configData: |
      core:
        sleepInterval: 60s
      sources:
        pci:
          deviceClassWhitelist: ["0200", "0300", "0302"]     # NICs, GPUs
          deviceLabelFields: [vendor, device]
        custom:
          - name: "network-sriov.capable"
            matchOn: [{pciId: {vendor: ["8086"], device: ["1593","158b"]}}]
```
Verify: `oc get node <n> --show-labels | tr ',' '\n' | grep feature.node`.

### 7.2 Node Maintenance Operator (NMO)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Puts a node into maintenance with a single CR: cordons, drains (respecting PDBs), and — with OpenShift Virtualization — live-migrates VMs. Reports drain progress and blocking pods. Safer and auditable compared with ad-hoc `oc adm drain`. |
| **Package** | `node-maintenance-operator` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-workload-availability` / all namespaces |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CR** | `NodeMaintenance` |

```yaml
apiVersion: nodemaintenance.medik8s.io/v1beta1
kind: NodeMaintenance
metadata: {name: worker-1-firmware}
spec:
  nodeName: worker-1
  reason: "BIOS/firmware update CHG0012345"
```
```bash
oc get nodemaintenance worker-1-firmware -o jsonpath='{.status.phase} {.status.pendingPods}'
# do the hardware work, then:
oc delete nodemaintenance worker-1-firmware   # uncordons
```
Production notes: pair with **Node Health Check** + **Self Node Remediation** operators (same `medik8s` family) if you want automated fencing of unresponsive bare-metal nodes.

### 7.3 Kernel Module Management (KMM)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Builds, signs (Secure Boot), and loads out-of-tree kernel modules on RHCOS nodes via a `Module` CR, with a DaemonSet per kernel version and automatic rebuild on cluster upgrades. Required for vendor drivers (NVIDIA pre-GPU-Operator, Intel QAT, FPGA, specialised NICs/HBAs). |
| **Package** | `kernel-module-management` (+ `kernel-module-management-hub` for ACM hub builds) |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-kmm` / all namespaces |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CRs** | `Module`, `PreflightValidationOCP` |

```yaml
apiVersion: kmm.sigs.x-k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Module
metadata: {name: vendor-nic, namespace: openshift-kmm}
spec:
  moduleLoader:
    container:
      modprobe: {moduleName: vendor_nic}
      kernelMappings:
        - regexp: '^.*\.x86_64$'
          containerImage: registry.example.com:8443/drivers/vendor-nic:${KERNEL_FULL_VERSION}
          build:
            dockerfileConfigMap: {name: vendor-nic-dockerfile}
          sign:
            keySecret: {name: secureboot-key}
            certSecret: {name: secureboot-cert}
            filesToSign: [/opt/lib/modules/${KERNEL_FULL_VERSION}/vendor_nic.ko]
  imageRepoSecret: {name: mirror-registry-pull}
  selector: {feature.node.kubernetes.io/pci-1234.present: "true"}
```
Production notes: run `PreflightValidationOCP` against the target kernel **before** every cluster upgrade; disconnected builds need the DTK (driver toolkit) image mirrored (`additionalImages: registry.redhat.io/openshift4/driver-toolkit-rhel9`).

