## 8. Multi-cluster — Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Hub for a fleet of clusters: lifecycle (create/import/upgrade clusters, incl. bare metal via Assisted Installer), **Governance** (policy-as-code enforcing operators, configs, and compliance across clusters), application placement (GitOps/ApplicationSets across clusters), **Observability** (Thanos-based long-term metrics across clusters), and **DR** (Regional-DR / Metro-DR with ODF). Install on a dedicated hub cluster, not the production workload cluster. |
| **Packages** | `advanced-cluster-management` (pulls `multicluster-engine`) |
| **Namespace / scope** | `open-cluster-management` / single namespace |
| **Channel** | `release-2.16` (check `defaultChannel`) |
| **Primary CRs** | `MultiClusterHub`, `ManagedCluster`, `Policy`, `PlacementBinding`, `MultiClusterObservability` |

```yaml
apiVersion: operator.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: MultiClusterHub
metadata: {name: multiclusterhub, namespace: open-cluster-management}
spec:
  availabilityConfig: High
  disableHubSelfManagement: false
  nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""}
  tolerations:
    - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
    - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
  overrides:
    components:
      - {name: cluster-backup, enabled: true}       # OADP-based hub backup
      - {name: search, enabled: true}
---
# Example governance policy: require Compliance Operator on all prod clusters
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Policy
metadata: {name: policy-compliance-operator, namespace: rhacm-policies}
spec:
  remediationAction: enforce
  disabled: false
  policy-templates:
    - objectDefinition:
        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
        kind: ConfigurationPolicy
        metadata: {name: compliance-operator-sub}
        spec:
          remediationAction: enforce
          severity: high
          object-templates:
            - complianceType: musthave
              objectDefinition:
                apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1alpha1
                kind: Subscription
                metadata: {name: compliance-operator, namespace: openshift-compliance}
                spec: {name: compliance-operator, channel: stable, source: cs-redhat-operator-index-v4-22, sourceNamespace: openshift-marketplace}
---
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1beta1
kind: Placement
metadata: {name: prod-clusters, namespace: rhacm-policies}
spec:
  predicates: [{requiredClusterSelector: {labelSelector: {matchLabels: {environment: prod}}}}]
---
apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementBinding
metadata: {name: bind-compliance, namespace: rhacm-policies}
placementRef: {name: prod-clusters, kind: Placement, apiGroup: cluster.open-cluster-management.io}
subjects: [{name: policy-compliance-operator, kind: Policy, apiGroup: policy.open-cluster-management.io}]
```
Import an existing cluster: console → Infrastructure → Clusters → Import, or `oc apply` the generated `ManagedCluster` + klusterlet manifests on the spoke.
Production notes: hub sizing ≈ 3 × 8 vCPU/32 GB infra just for ACM + Observability; disconnected hubs need the `multicluster-engine` and assisted-service images mirrored; use the Policy Generator Kustomize plugin from the open-cluster-management/policy-collection repo for policy-as-code.

