## 10. Service Mesh, Serverless, Virtualization (install only if required)

### 10.1 OpenShift Service Mesh 3 (Istio)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Istio-based mesh: automatic **mTLS** between services, fine-grained L7 authorization, traffic shaping (canary, retries, circuit breaking), and telemetry via Kiali (visualization) and Tempo (tracing). OSSM 3 uses the upstream Sail operator model (`Istio`, `IstioCNI` CRs) and ambient/sidecar modes. |
| **Packages** | `servicemeshoperator3`; `kiali-ossm`; plus `tempo-product` and `opentelemetry-product` for tracing |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-operators` / all namespaces (control plane in `istio-system`, CNI in `istio-cni`) |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CRs** | `Istio`, `IstioCNI`, `IstioRevision`, `Kiali`, `PeerAuthentication`, `AuthorizationPolicy`, `Gateway` |

```yaml
apiVersion: sailoperator.io/v1
kind: Istio
metadata: {name: default}
spec:
  namespace: istio-system
  version: v1.26.4                         # match the operator's supported version
  updateStrategy: {type: RevisionBased, inactiveRevisionDeletionGracePeriodSeconds: 30}
  values:
    meshConfig:
      accessLogFile: /dev/stdout
      defaultConfig: {holdApplicationUntilProxyStarts: true}
      extensionProviders:
        - name: otel-tracing
          opentelemetry: {service: otel-collector.openshift-tracing.svc, port: 4317}
    pilot: {autoscaleEnabled: true, autoscaleMin: 2}
---
apiVersion: sailoperator.io/v1
kind: IstioCNI
metadata: {name: default}
spec: {namespace: istio-cni, version: v1.26.4}
---
# Mesh-wide strict mTLS
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1
kind: PeerAuthentication
metadata: {name: default, namespace: istio-system}
spec: {mtls: {mode: STRICT}}
```
Add workloads: label namespace `istio-injection=enabled` (sidecar) or `istio.io/dataplane-mode=ambient`.
Production notes: significant CPU/memory overhead per pod in sidecar mode; introduce in `PERMISSIVE` mTLS and move to `STRICT` once all callers are in the mesh; the OpenShift router can front Istio ingress gateways with passthrough routes.

### 10.2 OpenShift Serverless (Knative)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | **Knative Serving** — scale-to-zero HTTP services with revision-based traffic splitting; **Knative Eventing** — event-driven architecture with Brokers/Triggers, Kafka source/sink, and CloudEvents; **Functions** — build/deploy functions via `kn func`. Use for bursty or event-driven workloads; otherwise skip. |
| **Package** | `serverless-operator` |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-serverless` / all namespaces |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CRs** | `KnativeServing` (ns `knative-serving`), `KnativeEventing` (ns `knative-eventing`), `KnativeKafka` |

```yaml
apiVersion: operator.knative.dev/v1beta1
kind: KnativeServing
metadata: {name: knative-serving, namespace: knative-serving}
spec:
  high-availability: {replicas: 2}
  ingress: {kourier: {enabled: true}}        # or istio: {enabled: true} with OSSM
  config:
    autoscaler: {enable-scale-to-zero: "true", scale-to-zero-grace-period: 30s, stable-window: 60s}
    defaults: {max-revision-timeout-seconds: "600", revision-timeout-seconds: "300"}
    deployment: {registries-skipping-tag-resolving: "registry.example.com:8443"}   # disconnected
    network: {domain-template: "{{.Name}}-{{.Namespace}}.{{.Domain}}", autocreate-cluster-domain-claims: "true"}
---
apiVersion: operator.knative.dev/v1beta1
kind: KnativeEventing
metadata: {name: knative-eventing, namespace: knative-eventing}
spec:
  high-availability: {replicas: 2}
  config:
    default-br-config: {clusterDefault: {brokerClass: Kafka, apiVersion: v1, kind: ConfigMap, name: kafka-broker-config, namespace: knative-eventing}}
```
Production notes: mirror the Knative component images (`registry.redhat.io/openshift-serverless-1/*`); Kafka-backed brokers need AMQ Streams (`amq-streams` operator); set `min-scale` annotations on latency-sensitive services.

### 10.3 OpenShift Virtualization (KubeVirt)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Runs KVM virtual machines as Kubernetes resources alongside containers: `VirtualMachine` CRs, live migration, VM templates, snapshots, hot-plug disks/NICs, and migration tooling (MTV) for importing from VMware/RHV/OVA. Requires bare metal (nested virt unsupported) with VT-x/AMD-V enabled and RWX storage (ODF RBD) for live migration. |
| **Package** | `kubevirt-hyperconverged` (+ `mtv-operator` for migrations) |
| **Namespace / scope** | `openshift-cnv` / single namespace |
| **Channel** | `stable` |
| **Primary CRs** | `HyperConverged`, `VirtualMachine`, `DataVolume`, `MigrationPolicy` |

```yaml
apiVersion: hco.kubevirt.io/v1beta1
kind: HyperConverged
metadata: {name: kubevirt-hyperconverged, namespace: openshift-cnv}
spec:
  infra:
    nodePlacement:
      nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/infra: ""}
      tolerations:
        - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoSchedule}
        - {key: node-role.kubernetes.io/infra, value: reserved, effect: NoExecute}
  workloads:
    nodePlacement:
      nodeSelector: {node-role.kubernetes.io/virt: ""}       # dedicated VM nodes
  liveMigrationConfig:
    parallelMigrationsPerCluster: 5
    parallelOutboundMigrationsPerNode: 2
    bandwidthPerMigration: 64Mi
    completionTimeoutPerGiB: 800
    progressTimeout: 150
  featureGates:
    enableCommonBootImageImport: false        # disconnected: upload boot sources manually
    deployKubeSecondaryDNS: false
  evictionStrategy: LiveMigrate
  certConfig: {ca: {duration: 48h0m0s, renewBefore: 24h0m0s}, server: {duration: 24h0m0s, renewBefore: 12h0m0s}}
  resourceRequirements:
    vmiCPUAllocationRatio: 4                  # overcommit ratio
```
Verify: `oc get hco -n openshift-cnv kubevirt-hyperconverged -o jsonpath='{.status.conditions}'`, `oc get nodes -l kubevirt.io/schedulable=true`.
Production notes: license Virtualization separately (core-based); VM networking usually needs NMState bridges (Section 6.2) + Multus NADs; use the Performance Profile for latency-sensitive VMs; the OpenShift Virtualization Engine SKU exists for VM-only clusters.

